  timelineLayout: true
  combinedSchedule: true
  days:
  - day: 1
    title: Lijiang Heritage In-Depth
    schedule:
    - period: ''
      activities:
      - Pickup at Lijiang Sanyi Airport (LJG) or your Old Town hotel, transfer to your boutique Naxi courtyard guesthouse. Afternoon at Black Dragon Pond Park with the iconic Moon-Embracing Pavilion and stunning views of Jade Dragon Snow Mountain, plus the Dongba Museum next door - Naxi pictographs and culture. Stroll through the lively Zhongyi Market and the cobblestone streets of Dayan Old Town. Welcome dinner.
  - day: 2
    title: Hidden Jade Dragon
    schedule:
    - period: ''
      activities:
      - Drive to the Wenhai Nature Reserve,stop for a cup of green tea at a local Naxi minority conservationist home. After home-cooked lunch in Yi minority village chiefs place, trek into the hidden trails of the Jade Dragon Snow Mountain Nature Reserve - off the rope-line, away from the cable car crowds,with local forest rangers, birdwatching and nature photography along the way. Return to Lijiang, dinner in Old Town.
  - day: 3
    title: Lashi Wetlands + Tiger Leaping Gorge + Shangri-La
    schedule:
    - period: ''
      activities:
      - Morning stop at Lashi Wetlands of International Importance - dawn crane flight, waterfowl, Black Drongo roosts. Continue north toward Shangri-La. Visit the legendary Tiger Leaping Gorge (Hutiaoxia) - one of the deepest river canyons on Earth. Arrive in mystical Shangri-La. Dukezong Old Town - the spiritual heart of Tibetan Yunnan. Dinner and overnight.
  - day: 4
    title: Songzanlin + Great Bend + Dongzhulin + Deqin
    schedule:
    - period: ''
      activities:
      - Visit the magnificent Songzanlin Monastery - the 'Little Potala Palace', a major centre of Tibetan Buddhism. Drive north via Benzilan to the dramatic Golden Sand River Great Bend. Visit the peaceful Dongzhulin Monastery. Arrive in Deqin - the gateway town to Meili Snow Mountain. Dinner and overnight in the snow-capped mountain setting.
  - day: 5
    title: Kawagebo Sunrise + Cizhong Village + Mekong Walk
    schedule:
    - period: ''
      activities:
      - Pre-dawn departure to the Feilai Monastery viewpoint for sunrise view of Kawagebo (6,740m) - Yunnan's highest peak. A clear-morning alpine glow that stays with you for years. Visit Cizhong Village on the Mekong River - the 100-year-old French Catholic church, still active, surrounded by Lisu-minority vineyards. Walk along the Mekong. Traditional dinner paired with local Cizhong wine. Overnight in Cizhong.
  - day: 6
    title: Tacheng Bee Farm
    schedule:
    - period: ''
      activities:
      - 'Drive to Tacheng in the Weixi highlands. Afternoon: visit a smallholder farm where Apis cerana ssp. cerana - the native Chinese honey bee - still forages on wild rhododendron and vitex at 2,500m. Sample honey that tastes like the flowers and the cold of the valley. Overnight in Tacheng.'
  - day: 7
    title: Snub-nosed Monkeys + First Bend  + Lijiang Return
    schedule:
    - period: ''
      activities:
      - Early departure to the Yunnan Snub-nosed Monkey National Park. Trek into the habitat to observe the critically endangered Yunnan Snub-nosed Monkeys (fewer than 4,000 in the world). Lunch at a local rainbow trout farm, then visit the Baima Snow Mountain Nature Conservation Bureau for insights into the conservation work. Drive south along the Yangtze, witness the dramatic First Bend of the Yangtze, arrive in Lijiang. Farewell dinner at a Naxi courtyard restaurant in Lijiang Old Town.
  - day: 8
    title: Free Time + Departure
    schedule:
    - period: ''
      activities:
      - Free time in Lijiang Old Town, then private transfer to the airport or train station at the time of your choice.
